+\paragraph{Complete original-path cost profile.}
+A separate instrumented capture returns all 29,750 GoedelWorkbook4.27 sources
+and retains body profiles for 29,689 of them. All 61 sources without a body
+profile have operational outcomes.
+The arithmetic prover \texttt{linarith}~\cite{mathlib} and its detailed regions
+have the largest recorded leaf-wall totals, followed by \texttt{simp}.
+These thresholded trace weights measure wall intervals that can overlap across
+threads and requests, rather than CPU fractions or device-eligible work.
+The observation characterizes the original arithmetic route.
+Residual costs after the strongest CPU route remain to be measured.
+
+\paragraph{Complete compiled-route CPU sampling.}
+A separate instrumented compiled-route run returns all 29,750 sources and
+retains 5,401,763 user-CPU samples with zero reported lost samples.
+Exclusive sample counts and periods reconcile across flat and callchain
+reports. Standard \texttt{perf} children weights include callees and
+overlap~\cite{perfReport}.
+Against all recorded user-CPU period, the displayed inclusive weights are
+35.00\% for the Meta definitional-equality export,
+16.96\% for a sparse-simplex certificate-oracle entry and
+10.81\% for a typeclass-synthesis entry.
+The first symbol is exported by a \texttt{MetaM} implementation in the
+installed Lean4.27 source~\cite{lean427MetaDefEq}; it is not a pure C++ kernel
+checking fraction. These entries cannot be added into disjoint phases.
+Separately, reference-count decrement and small allocation account for
+20.05\% of native exclusive recorded period; that pair is not an exhaustive
+runtime category. Sampling, unknowns and callchain limits remain, and neither
+view supplies whole-wall decomposition, a GPU ceiling or batching readiness.
+This capture characterizes the compiled original arithmetic route; residual
+costs after selecting a different strongest CPU composition remain open.
+
